ry></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEKI HIDEKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIGETA KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AIDA, TOSHIYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HASAKA, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HOSHI, TOMOAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUROIWA, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEKI, HIDEKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIGETA, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A device to feed semiconductor process gas changed in a large capacity gas container (21) to users after decompression, the gas container (21) comprising a cylindrical body part (22) and hemispherical parts (23, 23) at the opposite ends thereof, wherein, on the axis (25) of the cylindrical body part (22), one hemispherical part is provided with a gas charging port (26) and the other is provided with a gas outlet port (27), a charging valve (28) is connected to the gas charging port and a gas take-out unit (29) having at least a container valve (30) and a pressure reducing valve (32) is connected to the gas take-out port, and the gas container (21) is stored in a container (36) together with the charging valve (28) and the gas take-out unit (29).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un dispositif d'apport de gaz de traitement de semiconducteur transformé dans un conteneur (21) à gaz à grande capacité à l'intention des utilisateurs après décompression, ce conteneur (21) à gaz consistant en un corps cylindrique (22) présentant des parties hémisphériques (23, 24) sur ses extrémités opposées. Sur l'axe (25) du corps cylindrique (22), l'une des parties hémisphériques est pourvue d'un orifice (26) de chargement de gaz, la seconde partie étant pourvue d'un orifice (27) d'échappement de gaz, une valve (28) de chargement étant reliée à l'orifice de chargement de gaz et une unité (29) de reprise de gaz présentant au moins une valve (30) de conteneur et une valve (32) de réduction de pression étant reliée à l'orifice de reprise de gaz. Par ailleurs, ce conteneur (21) de gaz est disposé dans un autre conteneur (36), avec la valve (28) de chargement et l'unité (29) de reprise de gaz.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>